From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 22:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] luma: notifications live in the shelf

Owner request, 2026-09-18: a notification goes to the far right of the
shelf and lives there until it is handled. There are no banners at the top
of the screen any more.

The resting-notification beacon becomes the notifications island, the last
island of the shelf row, after Quick Options and its clock, which it pushes
towards the dock. It shows the newest unread notification compactly: the
application's mark, the title, the first line of the body, and a count
pill when more than one waits. Clicking the island opens the newest one;
the count opens the whole stack (the 0116 tray). Hovered or focused, the
body line gives way to up to two of the notification's actions and a
dismiss button, in slots that keep the island's width. A drag right of 72
px, or a fling past 24 px faster than 0.5 px/ms, dismisses the newest; a
shorter or slower drag springs back. Delete dismisses it from the keyboard.
Clearing the last one removes the island.

It grows in from the end of the row in 200 ms while the other islands slide
aside on the same curve, and reverses when it leaves. With reduced motion
it only fades (150 ms) and nothing slides.

An arriving notification goes straight to the island (it still chimes).
Urgent notifications and calls keep a card, which now sits above the
island at the end of the shelf. Lock-screen, full-screen, sharing and
casting rules are unchanged. With Quick Options hidden the island still
ends the row. A glyph mark is recognised by its -symbolic name before the
icon has loaded, so the first notification no longer shows its glyph bare.

The shelf keeps its islands by their ADR-044 ids ('dock', 'live',
'media', 'notifications', 'quick-options', 'aux'): Shelf.getIsland(id),
island.islandId, and the actor name lumaShelfIsland-<id>.

A shelf sync asked for from inside a sync (an island leaving the row stops
its transitions, whose handlers sync again) rebuilt the row while Clutter
was still walking its children, and the Shell aborted in
clutter_actor_remove_all_children. A nested request now runs once after the
running sync, and the row is emptied one island at a time from a copy.
